# Security testing

Test plan lives in `.security/TEST-PLAN.md`; conventions in
`integrations/foundry/README.md`.

- Every security requirement needs adversarial tests, not just happy paths:
  unauthorized-caller reverts (`test_RevertWhen_*`), boundary values
  (0, 1 wei, max), first/last-actor scenarios.
- Run tests through the framework so they become evidence:
  `security-check SEC-TEST-002` (suite), `SEC-TEST-003` (invariants) — not
  just bare `forge test`, which proves nothing to the ledger.
- Never weaken, skip, or delete a failing test to make a check pass. A
  failing security test is a finding: record it via the relevant
  `security-check` (the runner creates FND-* entries) and tell the user.
- Exploit tests live in `test/exploits/` and are permanent
  (`methodology/ADVERSARIAL-ANALYSIS.md`). Removing one invalidates
  SEC-TEST-004.
- Tests referenced by `.security/invariants.yaml` must keep their identifiers
  stable; renaming breaks traceability (SEC-PROC-003 will fail and point at
  the dangling reference).
